#: ../../hardware/controllers/behringer_ddm4000.md:91
msgid ""
"On some units of this mixer, the LEDs of the buttons {hwlabel}`P1` / "
"{hwlabel}`P2` / {hwlabel}`P3`   show an unexpected behavior in MIDI mode. "
"When such a LED is turned on via MIDI, it flashes   shortly but does not "
"stay lit. The problem occurs only when at least 1 channel is in audio   "
"(non-MIDI) mode. It does not occur when all channels are in MIDI mode.   "
"Firmware version 1.02 (Dec 14 2007) is known to show this behavior,   and "
"there's no fix available according to a reply from the technical support:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/behringer_ddm4000.md:98
msgid ""
"\"I see the issue, but sorry, the code is 15 years old and getting the 15 "
"year old tools  (plus license, plus old windows version) needed to compile "
"it,  together with finding the bug in a very complex code base (without "
"access to the developer)  makes fixing this nearly impossible.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/behringer_ddm4000.md:103
